 "status": "active",
 "title": "Acquisition checks B1-B8 and the per-sign B6b gates (as-measured scan)",
 "description": "Supported-input matrix (B1: LabSpec as8, Trek-type as7, FieldSpec 3 legacy reflectance; per-file detector joins) and the bad-scan checks on the AS-MEASURED reflectance (PLAN v3.2 Step 1-2). Unusable (B1-B4) replaces every verdict with Rescan. B6 is a Check only, raised per model when noise could carry the reading across a verdict cut (DECISIONS 109); never Unusable. B6b gates each contaminant sign (and C1) on the noise in its own window, with cuts keyed by the transfer applied to the stream. N2 is the canonical noise measure (1e-5 absorbance).",
 "licence": "CC-BY-4.0",
 "created": "2026-10-03",
 "provenance": {
  "basis": "SPYDER Bone planning reports 03 (reader), 07 (warnings), Phase 0a A1-A2 (canonical N2, B6b cut 60, correlated-noise gains). B8 thresholds from the relative splice steps of every file in hand (standard-resolution files <= 1.7%, high-resolution sessions <= 6.8%).",
  "per_sign_gates": "Phase 0c (high-resolution noise study): clean false alarms of each sign on 1,201 clean standard-resolution scans with high-resolution-like noise injected, after the v0.2 transfer, as a function of the noise in the sign's own window; cut = the largest N2 at which the false-alarm rate stays within +0.25 points of the noiseless rate (model noise shape; measured shape as the pessimistic bound): wax 80 / 59 -> 60, ester 306 / 215 -> 250, plaster 174 / 125 -> 150, C1 125 / 50 -> 125. Burnt (visible-range edge and short-wave OH bands) is ungated on v0.2; the 'none' table keeps the shipped gate so standard-resolution behaviour is unchanged.",
  "fallbacks": "2026-10-13 (pre-registered): the gates' cut N2(1500-1600) <= 30 (both fallbacks) is the largest noise at which the reduced statistics keep clean false alarms within the noiseless rate on 1,201 clean standard-resolution scans with high-resolution-like noise injected after the v0.2 transfer; 38 of 40 dark high-resolution scans pass it. Not N2(1400-1500) for plaster: the gypsum bands themselves raise it (median 17 -> 46-81 with plaster added), so that gate would close exactly when plaster is present (amendment 1)."
 },
