   "note": "A sign is gated (not checked) when N2 of its own window on the AS-MEASURED scan exceeds its cut; the table is picked by the transfer key of the standard-resolution stream ('none' or the transfer file's sha256); a key with no entry uses the 'none' table; a null gate means the sign is never gated (burnt on v0.2: it reads the visible edge, not the noisy SWIR2). A gated sign with a fallback for the key (fallbacks_by_transfer_key) runs its reduced variant instead when N2 of the fallback window is at most n2_at_most (plaster: the 1446 nm band alone, check.signs plaster.reduced_1446; C1: the variant below 1800 nm, check.c1 swir1); it then counts as checked. The record keeps check.B6b as a summary: n2 = N2(n2_window_nm), signs_gated = the contaminant signs gated with no fallback available (not checked), signs_reduced = the gated signs whose reduced variant is eligible (it runs, except C1 when a specific sign fired: C1 is then skipped as usual), gated = every contaminant sign in signs_gated, outcome Note when either list is non-empty."
